Subject: Keep Knative informer compatible with Kubernetes client-go 0.34

Origin: DHI-internal (KEDA 2.19 dependency compatibility)
Description: Preserve the informer construction used before WatchList semantics required client-go 0.35.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/knative/pkg 52dbd5ece63fe6d2d340ecbebec160550f460818 path=apis/duck
Verify: cmd `dhi def build image/keda-admission-webhooks/debian-13/2.19.yaml` expect "Successfully built"
Forwarded: not-needed (KEDA 2.19 pins Kubernetes client-go 0.34)
Drop-When: dependency k8s.io/client-go >= v0.35.4

KEDA 2.19 pins client-go 0.34 while the updated Knative module calls an API introduced in client-go 0.35. Reusing the previous ListWatch implementation keeps KEDA's Kubernetes dependency line unchanged.

--- a/apis/duck/typed.go
+++ b/apis/duck/typed.go
@@ -54,12 +54,10 @@ func (dif *TypedInformerFactory) Get(ctx context.Context, gvr schema.GroupVersio
 	}
 
 	listObj := dif.Type.GetListType()
-	rawLW := &cache.ListWatch{
+	lw := &cache.ListWatch{
 		ListWithContextFunc:  asStructuredLister(dif.Client.Resource(gvr).List, listObj),
 		WatchFuncWithContext: AsStructuredWatcher(dif.Client.Resource(gvr).Watch, dif.Type),
 	}
-	// Wrap with standard K8s function to properly handle WatchList semantics detection
-	lw := cache.ToListWatcherWithWatchListSemantics(rawLW, dif.Client)
 	inf := cache.NewSharedIndexInformer(lw, dif.Type, dif.ResyncPeriod, cache.Indexers{
 		cache.NamespaceIndex: cache.MetaNamespaceIndexFunc,
 	})
